  "body": "Auction: 8-12 The Promenade, Takapuna on Wednesday 9 December 2026 at 9:30AM  (unless sold prior)\r\n\r\nThe view is already done. Waitemata Harbour sweeping across to Rangitoto, ships and yachts coming and going, and a sky that puts on a different show every morning. This is the first time 1/64 Beach Road has been offered for sale since the 1990s, and the rest is yours to shape.\r\n\r\nSet on Beach Road in Castor Bay, the home looks straight out over the harbour to Rangitoto Island. It is the outlook buyers on this stretch of coast pay for, and it is the one thing no renovation can add. Everything else can be changed.\r\n\r\nAround 280sqm (approx) of floor area gives you real room to spread out:\r\n• 4 bedrooms and 2 bathrooms including an ensuite\r\n• 2 separate living areas, one for the family and one for everyone else\r\n• Separate dining area with mesmerising sea views\r\n• Under-house storage, with potential to do more\r\n• A sauna attached to the main bathroom\r\n• Harbour and Rangitoto views from the main living spaces\r\n• Extensive wrap around decking and a private backyard\r\n\r\nAfter decades in the same hands, the home needs modernising, and that is the opportunity. A 280sqm (approx) canvas with the harbour and Rangitoto views already in place gives a buyer with vision the chance to create something special. Renovated homes along this coast are marketed on the strength of their outlook; this one already has the outlook, and you get to write the rest yourself. Take on the project and the reward is yours.\r\n\r\nFamilies are well placed here, with zoning for Campbells Bay School, Wairau Intermediate and Murrays Bay Intermediate, and Westlake Boys & and Westlake Girls & High Schools.\r\n\r\nWalk to Castor Bay Beach for a morning swim, then carry on along the coastal walkway to Kennedy Park and its clifftop tracks and old WWII bunkers. Milford Beach and Campbells Bay Beach are close by, and a local cafe is just down the road. Milford village has the cafes, restaurants and shops for everything else, and the motorway is a short drive away. It is the coastal lifestyle people move to the East Coast Bays for: sand under your feet before breakfast, a harbour outlook at dinner, and everything within a few minutes.\r\n\r\nHomes with this much space and sweeping sea views are tightly held, and one that has not been offered in over thirty years rarely comes back.\r\n\r\nNote: some photos have been digitally de-cluttered.",
